 "# ADR-2607061700: cloud-itonami-vc-fund — venture capital fund blueprint (DD-LLM ⊣ InvestmentCommitteeGovernor)\n\n**Status**: accepted  \n**Date**: 2026-07-06  \n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Decision\n\n1. New standalone blueprint `cloud-itonami-vc-fund`, published outside ISIC numbering (precedent: `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-cofog-*`), because ISIC codes 6420 (holding companies)/6430 (trust/fund vehicle, excludes management)/6499 (own-account investment incl. venture capital companies, per UN ISIC Rev.4 explanatory note)/6630 (fee-based fund management) are all already published, differently-scoped `cloud-itonami-isic-*` repos — none can host a new VC blueprint without overwriting live content, and no single one of them covers the full VC lifecycle anyway (a real VC firm spans fund-vehicle + management-fee + own-account-carry-investing simultaneously).\n2. `kotoba-lang/industry`'s `registry.edn` is NOT modified — stays a strict ISIC Rev.4-only ledger (643/643), same as every other non-ISIC cloud-itonami-* family.\n3. Actor pair `DD-LLM ⊣ InvestmentCommitteeGovernor`, direct template port of `cloud-itonami-isic-6511`'s Underwriter-LLM ⊣ UnderwritingGovernor (langgraph-clj StateGraph, sealed advisor, independent governor, phase 0→3 rollout). Ops: `:lp/intake` (LP募集), `:kyc/screen` (AML/sanctions, LPs + portfolio-company parties), `:dd/assess` (DD checklist vs named framework spec-basis), `:investment/commit` (運用 — capital deployment, actuation), `:exit/distribute` (exit — proceeds + LP waterfall, actuation). Two actuation members (not one, unlike the insurance template) because a VC fund has two independent real-money-movement directions.\n4. HARD checks: spec-basis, sanctions-hit, DD-incomplete (carried over from the insurance template) plus one new VC-specific HARD check, `accredited-investor-violation` (blocks `:investment/commit` when an LP has no recorded accredited-investor/QP affirmation — a genuine Reg D / Investment Company Act requirement). `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami` ADR-0010's non-equity guard (`guard-non-equity!`) does NOT carry over — this repo assumes real securities compliance applies, the opposite posture, matching how the insurance blueprint assumes a real insurance license applies.\n5. Facts catalog seeds the same 4 jurisdictions as `cloud-itonami-isic-6511` (JPN QII exemption/FSA, USA Reg D+ILPA+NVCA, GBR FCA sub-threshold AIFMD, DEU BaFin/KAGB+EuVECA), honest coverage reporting.\n6. Waterfall distribution (`vcfund.registry/distribute-waterfall`) is deal-by-deal, not a real whole-fund European waterfall with GP clawback — documented limitation, not silent.\n7. Maturity `:implemented` from R0 per owner's explicit choice: full Clojure governed-actor implementation + tests, matching `cloud-itonami-isic-6511`'s bar, not blueprint-markdown-only.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) Answers the owner's original question with running code: LP intake → DD → capital deployment → exit distribution, each step governed and audited.\n- (+) `kotoba-lang/industry`'s ISIC-only invariant stays intact.\n- (+) Reuses the fleet-proven actor architecture rather than inventing a new one.\n- (−) R0 seeds only 4 of ~194 jurisdictions' fund-formation/exemption regimes — reported honestly, not claimed as global.\n- (−) Deal-by-deal waterfall, not whole-fund European waterfall with clawback.\n- (−) Real accredited-investor verification, real KYC/AML provider integration, real cap-table/fund-accounting integration are out of scope, same as every sibling :implemented entry.\n- Registration: published standalone under the `cloud-itonami` GitHub org (public, AGPL-3.0-or-later); NOT added to `manifest/west.yml` (this whole fleet is intentionally outside west management); noted only as a doc-comment in `manifest/repos.edn`, matching the `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-cofog-*` precedent.\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- blueprint repo (cloud-itonami org, public, AGPL-3.0-or-later, :implemented maturity): cloud-itonami-vc-fund\n\n## References\n\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-6511` ADR-0001 — the direct template this ADR ports.\n- ADR-2607012000 / ADR-2607031600 — precedent for non-ISIC-numbered blueprint families outside `kotoba-lang/industry`'s registry.\n- `gftdcojp/cloud-itonami` ADR-0010 — the non-equity design this repo deliberately does not reuse.\n- UN ISIC Rev.4 code 6499: https://unstats.un.org/unsd/classifications/Econ/Detail/EN/27/6499 (verified 2026-07-06).\n- 本 ADR とペアの .md\n\n## Addendum (2026-07-06, same day): consolidated into cloud-itonami-isic-6499\n\nOwner pushed back on the non-ISIC standalone naming and asked to reconsider 6499's availability. `cloud-itonami-isic-6499` (published 2026-07-04) turned out to be a two-commit, zero-fork, zero-star, code-free :blueprint scaffold illustrated with a different n.e.c. example (factoring/check-cashing/money-order) — not meaningfully occupied, and 6499's own explanatory note names venture capital first. Reversed the \"Alternatives considered\" decision: (1) replaced cloud-itonami-isic-6499's README/blueprint.edn/docs/GOVERNANCE/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY with the venture-fund description and moved the full vcfund.* src/test/deps.edn in as-is (namespace unchanged), re-verified 33 tests/153 assertions + lint clean in the new location, pushed; (2) deleted the standalone cloud-itonami-vc-fund repo (existed under an hour, same session); (3) promoted kotoba-lang/industry's registry.edn \"6499\" entry :blueprint→:implemented (required-technologies :banking→:securities) via worktree branch + server-side merge (shared west checkout was in detached HEAD, per 並行エージェント運用 convention), updated docs/cloud-itonami.md's tier counts and test/kotoba/industry_test.clj's hardcoded :implemented count (4→5), re-verified 7 tests/53 assertions; (4) advanced manifest/west.yml's industry pin via `bb scripts/gen-west-manifest.bb --entry industry` (single-entry, server-verified fast-forward); (5) updated manifest/repos.edn's doc-comment to point at the consolidated cloud-itonami-isic-6499 entry. The original decision text above is left unedited as the historical record of the first attempt. Net effect: one venture-capital-fund actor at cloud-itonami-isic-6499, :implemented maturity, ISIC-numbered like every sibling blueprint, no dangling standalone repo."}
